y put us to  hell i want to say the word that day and  i think we needed an explanation it  should have been done  months ago onslow belmont fire brigade  chief greg  muse and deputy chief darrell curry were  inside when the shots rang out at 10  21 a.m across the street a neighbor saw  an unmarked car  stop on the highway the two doors swung  open  two people ran towards the fire hall  one went in the ditch one went behind  the  garbage bin and they just  opened fire the mounties shot toward the  main entrance of the fire hall damaging  the building and a fire  truck inside the shots flew past another  rcmp officer standing next to a marked  cruiser  and an emergency management office  coordinator who was wearing a reflective  vest  it's believed the mounties mistook one  of them for the gunman  gabriel wartman was driving a mock  cruiser and wearing a police uniform and  vest  at the time he killed 22 people over 13  hours on april 18th and 19  2020. surveillance video viewed by  global news  shows the two mounties spent less than  two minutes on the property after the  shooting  and for an hour the men inside the hall  say no one told them  that the shooters were the police we  were terrorized for  one hour by the rcmp  in the middle of the worst mass shooting  in canadian history  curry and muse say the rcmp has never  apologized  the rcmp won't comment on the shooting  at the fire hall citing an ongoing  investigation by nova scotia's  independent police watchdog the serious  incident response team donna  okay sarah richie in halifax thanks  ahead myanmar's pro-democracy  protest endures in the face of the  bloodiest day yet  defiance in the face of a fierce police  crackdown in myanmar that killed 18  people on sunday  hundreds of demonstrators clashed with  security forces in the country's largest  city again today  demanding the elected government be  restored and ousted leader aung sang  made her first appearance since the coup  appearing in court via video